WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.700
What the...? Huh?

3
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.860
Uh! Buncha fools!

4
00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.300
Why did you have to get
all sentimental like that?

5
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.970
Now we can't cash in on his bounty!

6
00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:37.310
<b>Dive, Dive, Dive!</b>

7
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.300
If you don't get out of our way,
we'll arrest every last one of you!

8
00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.570
I'd like to see you try!

9
00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.340
Just let the man play his
rock n' roll damn it!

10
00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.110
Hey, what's going on over there?

11
00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.850
It's outta control,
I'll tell you that much!

12
00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.280
The Navy came to arrest Soul King during
his show and now his fans are rioting!

13
00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.390
Looks like he made his escape, though.

14
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.760
You skinless traitor!
I'm gonna make you pay!

15
00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.530
Anyway, that's not the big story here.

16
00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.500
Soul King is actually a pirate
known as the Humming Swordsman.

17
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.700
He's one of the Straw Hats!

18
00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.730
Thank you for the ride, my friend.

19
00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.940
And that was impeccable
timing, I must say!

20
00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.070
You can thank Shakky for
puttin' all this together.

21
00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.440
Your friends should be waiting
for you at Grove 42.

22
00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.080
I'm so eager to see them again,
my heart is beating out of my chest.

23
00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.220
Kidding. Obviously,
my chest is an empty void!

24
00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:33.760
<b>Grove 41</b>

25
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.430
So, here's the skinny, brother.

26
00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:34.630
Luffy's on the island, somewhere,
but the Navy's about to close in,

27
00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.280
and the rest of the crew
is headed to Grove 42.

28
00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.120
Meet us there.

29
00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.220
Roger that, Franky.

30
00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:39.990
Cu-lick.

31
00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.890
What's up?

32
00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.620
Great. You mean you weren't listening?

33
00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.660
Well, let's see.

34
00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:50.990
Navy, come here.
Us pirates, ship. Run away.

35
00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.190
Is that clear enough?

36
00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.520
Why are you talking like that?!

37
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.460
Did you hit your head or somethin'?

38
00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:59.490
Sorry. I just thought I'd
speak on your level for once.

39
00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.290
Huh?!

40
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.260
All right then. After this,
stupid cook die.

41
00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.660
Real funny.

42
00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.900
Anyway, you know what all the
racket over there's about?

43
00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:09.630
Huh?

44
00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:14.840
You, right. Noisy, there.

45
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.580
All right, that's
enough yakking! Listen!

46
00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.650
Turns out Sanji and Zoro found
one of the guys who insulted me.

47
00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.810
In fact, he's here with us right now!

48
00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.090
Look at this little punk!

49
00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:40.230
I'm gonna beat a lesson into
him with my own two hands!

50
00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:44.230
'Cause when you piss me off,
then things get ugly!

51
00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.390
And let this be a lesson
to all of you, too.

52
00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.720
If you ever cross me,
if you ever disrespect me,

53
00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.990
you're gonna end up
just like this chump!

54
00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.230
Don't forget who's
the boss of this crew!

55
00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.890
Is that perfectly clear?

56
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.290
He earned that bounty somehow,
and it wasn't by playing nicey-nice.

57
00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.920
What's with this guy?

58
00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.230
Zoro, Sanji, he a friend
of yours or somethin'?

59
00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.790
'Cause I don't think he likes me.

60
00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.900
We've got you surrounded!
Nobody move an inch!

61
00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.170
Straw Hat Luffy, you and the rest
of your crew are under arrest!

62
00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.850
Surrender immediately!

63
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.120
The Navy?

64
00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.690
And don't bother running away.

65
00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.990
We've blocked off
every exit in Grove 46.

66
00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:23.860
You guys leave with us,

67
00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.240
or you're gonna leave in a body bag!

68
00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.810
But my disguise is perfect.

69
00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.080
How did the Navy know I was here?

70
00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:30.950
What? Why would you think
this was about you?

71
00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.550
Captain, please tell me
we're not all dead.

72
00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.720
Stop flippin' out. We'll be just fine!

73
00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.960
Why do you think we
recruited all these guys?

74
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.120
We've got pirates with
100 million bounties here!

75
00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.490
But this is scary.

76
00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.690
Then sit back and watch!

77
00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.440
Heh.

78
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.940
Caribou, you're up!

79
00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.280
Use that Marine as a shield and
make us a path outta this dump!

80
00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.620
Wait, what Marine?

81
00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.250
We sent a scout here earlier,
and it looks like he was taken captive.

82
00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.690
Dammit, that's not good.

83
00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.520
What the hell are you doin', Caribou?

84
00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.160
We need him to escape!
Did you even hear me?

85
00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.430
Although that would be
terribly convenient,

86
00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.800
I'm afraid it simply won't do.

87
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:06.870
Why not?

88
00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.620
and that makes him
a filthy little liar.

89
00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.260
Because he told me he hadn't
called the Navy yet,

90
00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:15.760
Caribou, no!

91
00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.740
That crazy bastard!

92
00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.330
Who's the captain here, damn it?

93
00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:32.240
Oh, well. So much for that plan.

94
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.700
You high and mighty types
seem to think it's all right

95
00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.570
to lie to someone if they're
a so-called "bad guy."

96
00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.440
Well, I object to that.

97
00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.840
I guess they're not surrendering, huh?

98
00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.840
Should've figured as much.

99
00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.150
Charge! Show the pirates no mercy!

100
00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:51.220
Good luck! Our boss is Straw Hat Luffy.

101
00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:54.390
He's not gonna lose to a buncha
chumps like you! Let's go!

102
00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.770
If you've got a plan, I'd hurry!

103
00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.010
Listen to your captain!
You guys're pissing me off!

104
00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:06.840
That guy just said that I was his boss,
but I've never even seen him before.

105
00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.610
I do not have time to deal
with your nonsense right now.

106
00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.770
Aim for their captain and charge!

107
00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.030
I know you.

108
00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:30.830
You're "Lip-Service" Doughty.
Your bounty's 88 million!

109
00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.740
You may be idiots, but at
least you're not cowards.

110
00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.940
Don't let him intimidate you! Uh!

111
00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:42.420
Holy crap.

112
00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:46.980
He's got a bounty of 92 million.
That's "Gashed" Albion!

113
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.340
We'll take them down!
Justice is on our side!

114
00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.620
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

115
00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.880
The ground is soaked with
the blood of hypocrites.

116
00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.710
Its overwhelming stench
makes me so sick.

117
00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:02.640
A 210 million bounty,
"Wet-Haired" Caribou!

118
00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:03.380
Huh?

119
00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.270
Too late to surrender now!

120
00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.280
Uh!

121
00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.180
Damn it, no one said he
had a Devil Fruit power!

122
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.180
Why don't we all slow down a bit?

123
00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.720
Haven't you heard that stress
can lead to an early grave?

124
00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.590
My sword!

125
00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:38.030
Nobody told me they were gonna be here.

126
00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.760
I kinda wanna beat up those robot guys,

127
00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.610
but Hancock said to stay outta
trouble, so I guess I won't.

128
00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:47.910
Those things'd vaporize the mustache
off your stupid face, you nutbag!

129
00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.800
Monkey D. Luffy has been
identified. Commence attack.

130
00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.070
Those things are aiming straight at me!

131
00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:02.180
Can I even run or am I just dead?

132
00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.910
I was hopin' I'd get to
rumble with them someday!

133
00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:13.510
"Lip-Service" Doughty
identified and subdued.

134
00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.340
Sustained no damage.
Searching for next target.

135
00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.940
Captain Doughty!

136
00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:24.240
Follow the Pacifistas! Capture
every pirate in your path!

137
00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.470
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

138
00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:26.740
Doughty's out cold!

139
00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:29.910
A bounty like that and these guys
took him down in only one shot?

140
00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.080
We're screwed.

141
00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.530
Hey, Captain, wait for us! Dang it!

142
00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.130
I ain't waiting for nobody!

143
00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:39.200
That thing took out Doughty!
I don't stand a chance!

144
00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.280
Straw Hat, do something!

145
00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.110
You're the only one
who can stop them now!

146
00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:52.150
I hate to beg, Captain, but your whole
crew is about to get blown up over here!

147
00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:54.890
There's nowhere left to run!

148
00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:57.450
Huh? Aw, crap, he's gone!

149
00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.280
Where is Straw Hat?

150
00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.750
They keep calling for
their captain, but...

151
00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.720
Slow down, you guys.
My side is killing me!

152
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.730
Screw your side! The lasers
are gonna kill you!

153
00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.560
Get your fat ass out of my way!

154
00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.130
Huh? Who is this idiot?

155
00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:16.650
He's here!

156
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.260
Captain Luffy!

157
00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.440
Am I mistaken, or did they
call you "Captain Luffy"?

158
00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.970
Why wouldn't they call me that?

159
00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:31.870
I mean, you realize who you're
talking to right now, don't you?

160
00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:36.010
Go! Get outta my way before I grab your
intestines and pull them out your ear!

161
00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:37.640
I'd run if I were you!

162
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:41.150
You're face-to-face with the son
of Dragon the Revolutionary!

163
00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:44.090
That means I'm the grandson
of the hero Garp!

164
00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:46.160
Oh, and my bounty?

165
00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.660
It clocks in at 400
million berries! I'm...

166
00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.370
You're not Straw Hat,
you human pile of garbage.

167
00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:56.030
Not even close!

168
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.110
Huh?

169
00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.510
Uh?

170
00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:04.110
– What?!
– What?!

171
00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:07.180
That guy just took out Straw Hat!

172
00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.550
So that's it. Fools.

173
00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:14.290
They thought that they could join
the Straw Hats and enter the New World.

174
00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.020
PX-5, who is this imposter?

175
00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.630
Confirmed. He is
"Triple-Tongued" Demaro Black.

176
00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.140
A pirate with a 26
million berry bounty.

177
00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.470
Wait, if he's only worth
26 million, that means...

178
00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.580
– He's a fake?!
– He's a fake?!

179
00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.830
Book it, guys! The jig is up!

180
00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.470
What the hell are we
supposed to do now?

181
00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.010
It's bad enough that
this guy tricked us,

182
00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.610
but now he got the
Navy called on us, too?!

183
00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:45.980
Guess the real Straw
Hat is dead after all.

184
00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:49.320
What the hell?! You mean Straw
Hat didn't get fat and gross?

185
00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.650
This guy was just fat
and gross to begin with?

186
00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.360
Wait, what?

187
00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:56.000
That fat gross guy was
pretending to be me?

188
00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:01.030
That Sanji and Zoro... they looked real,
but I guess they were fakes, too.

189
00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.480
Wow, this is blowin' my mind.
I gotta get out of here.

190
00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.850
I know you aren't real Straw Hats
and you're just victims of this fool,

191
00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.310
but you're still pirates.

192
00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:12.150
That means the lot of you
are coming with us!

193
00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:18.560
And although I cannot imagine why,
the real Straw Hat is here somewhere, too.

194
00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:23.960
When we entered the area, PX-5 detected
him on the stage with the imposters.

195
00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:26.430
Fire on Straw Hat, PX-5!

196
00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.440
That was close!

197
00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.650
You almost blew up my all my lunches!

198
00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.730
What did food ever do to you?

199
00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.990
It's... It's really him, isn't it?

200
00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:58.040
– That's Straw Hat Luffy!
– That's Straw Hat Luffy!

201
00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.310
The real Straw Hat was here
and we didn't even know?

202
00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.480
Nothing has changed, men!

203
00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.310
We came here to capture Straw
Hat and that's what we're doing!

204
00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:09.010
– Sir!
– Sir!

205
00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.210
So there you are!

206
00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:14.270
Agh! I had enough of you
the last time we fought!

207
00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.840
I'm just tryin' to set sail!

208
00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.900
I'm not supposed to start any trouble!

209
00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.440
Oh, it's no trouble,
but you won't be setting sail.

210
00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:25.010
Unlike two years ago, I'm an
official Navy officer now.

211
00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.060
That means I'm taking you in
if it's the last thing I do!

212
00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.790
PX-5, fire!

213
00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:39.290
Is that all?

214
00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:43.870
What?

215
00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.240
Second Gear.

216
00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:59.100
You're way too slow.

217
00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:10.470
Gum-Gum... Jet Pistol!

218
00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.110
This is worse than I thought.
He can use Haki now.

219
00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:28.420
– He beat a Pacifista! And all it took was one punch!
– He beat a Pacifista! And all it took was one punch!

220
00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.700
Though I have a feeling I'm
gonna see you again somewhere!

221
00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.100
Get back here and fight me!

222
00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:44.300
Don't let him go, men! Hurry!

223
00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:45.540
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

224
00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:50.150
Hey! Luffy!

225
00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.660
Luffy! Shoulda known!

226
00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.730
All I had to do was
follow the explosions

227
00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.400
Ah!

228
00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:00.600
Okay, it's you for real this time!

229
00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.480
This Zoro's not even fat! Way to go!

230
00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.350
Roronoa and Black Foot.

231
00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:07.080
I should've known
they were still alive.

232
00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.350
All right, PX-7, attack!

233
00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:10.350
– Huh?
– Huh?

234
00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.900
– Get lost!
– Get lost!

235
00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:25.640
I'm the one who got him.

236
00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:28.010
Keep dreaming! My kick broke his neck!

237
00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.290
It's the real Straw Hats!
They're monsters!

238
00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:36.800
The fake ones were nothing
like this at all!

239
00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.730
By the way, Luffy, you're number nine.

240
00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.900
Nobody cares! Would
you give up on that?!

241
00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:48.330
Everyone's waiting at the
Sunny. Let's get moving.

242
00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:49.170
Got it!

243
00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:54.440
We're not missing this chance!
Every last Marine, after them!

244
00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:55.240
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

245
00:15:55.820 --> 00:16:00.220
Man, it's been forever, huh?
I bet everyone's so cool now!

246
00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:01.860
I can't wait to see!

247
00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:03.390
Ha! Uh.

248
00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:10.850
What happened? Let's go!

249
00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.350
Ah.

250
00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:20.860
Rayleigh!

251
00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:23.190
It can't be.

252
00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:25.400
I came to check on you,

253
00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.420
but it seems you have
this under control.

254
00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:36.360
In fact, you're even stronger
than when I left you.

255
00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.630
Uh-huh!

256
00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.730
Finally time to see your friends.

257
00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:42.530
You've been waiting for long enough.

258
00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:44.700
Thanks, Rayleigh. For real.

259
00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.440
You did so much for me
these past two years!

260
00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:51.260
Ha-ha. No need
to get sappy on me. Just go.

261
00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:58.480
Hm?

262
00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:01.470
One last thing.

263
00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.640
I'm gonna do it.

264
00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:13.860
I'm gonna be the King of the Pirates!

265
00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.430
You hear me?!

266
00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.730
Uh! What are you doing?

267
00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.570
Hurry up and capture them already!

268
00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.450
Gotta move, Luffy!

269
00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.350
We appreciate the help, Rayleigh!

270
00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:40.020
Well, we're off!

271
00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:42.560
Thanks again for everything.

272
00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:45.290
See ya! I'm outta here!

273
00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.190
Good luck.

274
00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.750
Let nothing stop you
from reaching the top!

275
00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:23.790
The Straw Hats are making
a beeline for Grove 42!

276
00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.860
Catch them at any cost!

277
00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.790
The hell?

278
00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:36.100
Dark King Rayleigh.

279
00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.200
Why don't you just let the boy sail?

280
00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.870
He's been out of the game,
so take it easy.

281
00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:45.480
Uh. That's an intense line.

282
00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:49.310
If you think that's intense,
then why don't you try crossing it?

283
00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:57.560
Whoa! That's a lot!
You really went all out!

284
00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.520
What's inside?

285
00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:01.310
It's our food stock.

286
00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.450
I bought in bulk 'cause I'm
sure everyone's stomachs

287
00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:05.920
have gotten bigger
over these two years.

288
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.740
This should keep us
all happy for a while.

289
00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:11.270
Good thinking! I haven't had
your cooking in way too long!

290
00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:13.660
Over here! We found them!

291
00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:17.800
Crap! They got ahead of us somehow!

292
00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.800
Looks like we're gonna have
to fight our way through!

293
00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.700
Charge in! We've got this!

294
00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.140
Huh?

295
00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:29.690
I'm as worthless as a flea.

296
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.220
What's wrong? Get up before...

297
00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:36.150
Oh, no! What happened to their morale?

298
00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.840
I... I am nothing but a louse.

299
00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.370
This sure looks familiar.

300
00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.420
How did I know it was
you guys causing that ruckus?

301
00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:58.850
So typical.

302
00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:03.520
You're fooling around with the Navy
when you should've been gone long ago!

303
00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:06.920
Whoa! Well, aren't you
a sight for sore eyes?

304
00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:08.470
We know her?

305
00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:09.780
Speak for yourself!

306
00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:12.040
If you were smart,
you would've bailed by now!

307
00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:15.880
You wouldn't even be here if it
weren't for me, so don't start, mister!

308
00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.580
Who knows where you would've
wound up on your own?

309
00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.410
The least you could do is be gracious!

310
00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.600
She's an actual woman.
With real life girly parts!

311
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:29.300
Of course I am! What the hell
is your damage, you freak?

312
00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:31.600
All right, enough of this.
You guys need to get moving.

313
00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.000
There's Navy ships nearby,
so you're running out of time!

314
00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:37.590
If you don't get out of here
soon, you'll never escape.

315
00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:42.460
<b>The Straw Hats' Rendezvous Point, Grove 42 Shore</b>

316
00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.800
All right! You're here!

317
00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:58.900
What a surprise!

318
00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:01.640
I didn't think you'd
abandon stardom! Attaboy!

319
00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.540
Nothing could keep me from coming back.

320
00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.370
I've missed you all so.

321
00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:10.910
I see that you two have only
grown lovelier in our time apart.

322
00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:17.550
With all that in mind,
there's something I need to know.

323
00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.600
Ooh. It's already song time, huh?

324
00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.000
Please, Nami.
May I look at your panties?

325
00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:29.830
No way in hell!

326
00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:33.000
I never let you look at them two years
ago, why would I let you see them now?

327
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.570
Right. I was just excited to see you.

328
00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:37.230
It made my soul shake.

329
00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.770
And it's still shaking right now.

330
00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.840
In fact, it's about to leak
out of my ear, I think...

331
00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:44.250
I didn't think you could have
a muscle spasm without any muscles.

332
00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.580
Seriously?

333
00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:49.580
How is it none of you have grown
up after all of this time?

334
00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:54.700
Rejection aside, I was actually
expecting to be the last one here.

335
00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:58.170
Don't worry, Chopper is off
looking for our missing companions.

336
00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:58.630
Hey!

337
00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:07.660
Talk about perfect timing!

338
00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:10.430
Guys!

339
00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:14.870
Hey!

340
00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:23.430
Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!

341
00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:25.660
Hey!

342
00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:31.590
Together again! I've been
waiting for this day!

343
00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:34.500
And everyone looks stronger! I like it!

344
00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:38.670
It feels like it's been forever!

345
00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:46.760
Looks like we're the last... Hi, guys!

346
00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:55.680
Huh?

347
00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.230
He's hemorrhaging!

348
00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:08.190
Thanks a lot for the ride!

349
00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:10.760
Tell everyone back in the
Birdie Kingdom I say "hi."

350
00:23:12.610 --> 00:23:14.810
How is he? Has the
bleeding stopped yet?

351
00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:18.010
Not one... but two beautiful
women in front of me...

352
00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:20.570
Stay with me, man. Don't give up yet!

353
00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:23.370
It's no good, Chopper! He's
getting paler by the second!

354
00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:28.080
Ah! You... look... so cool, Franky!

355
00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.510
Yeah, you think so? Good!

356
00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:34.340
But even if you didn't, I could
change my style at will. Mecha!

357
00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:36.140
"Mecha"? Let me try!

358
00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.470
Okay, focus!

359
00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.840
This is no time to be fooling around!

360
00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:43.580
We need to get outta here while we
can before the Navy's on top of us!

361
00:23:46.160 --> 00:23:50.160
No, it looks like we're too late!

362
00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:52.200
I see three Navy ships.

363
00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:58.470
If we don't do something fast,
we're gonna be dead in the water!

364
00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:01.710
Fire! Sink that ship at all costs!

365
00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:15.440
What? They stopped in midair.

366
00:24:15.930 --> 00:24:18.100
Wait. Captain.

367
00:24:20.540 --> 00:24:22.580
It's the Kuja Pirates!

368
00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:28.010
Answer me this, knaves.

369
00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:34.520
Which one of you had the audacity
to place your disgusting ship in my path?

370
00:24:42.120 --> 00:24:44.590
That flag... It can't be.

371
00:24:44.590 --> 00:24:45.860
You know it?

372
00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:47.260
That's the Kuja symbol.

373
00:24:47.260 --> 00:24:50.760
They're a strong crew of Amazonians
lead by one of the Seven Warlords.

374
00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:51.760
You're joking, right?

375
00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:54.030
Not at all. Her name is Boa Hancock.

376
00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:55.930
They say anyone who lays eyes on her

377
00:24:55.930 --> 00:24:59.540
will be enamored by her beauty and turned
to stone, unless she grants you mercy.

378
00:24:59.540 --> 00:25:02.070
Whoa! Oh, I can see why!

379
00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:03.900
Beauty starts and ends with her!

380
00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:05.630
If I had eyes, they'd be sparkling!

381
00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:08.620
Oh, wow! She's like
a real-life goddess!

382
00:25:10.860 --> 00:25:11.830
Is she really that fine? Lemme see!

383
00:25:12.230 --> 00:25:14.960
My goddess. Where? Gotta find her.

384
00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:17.430
I wanna see. I wanna. I wanna.

385
00:25:18.770 --> 00:25:20.370
He's as hard as a rock!

386
00:25:21.070 --> 00:25:22.930
Hancock said she wasn't comin' here.

387
00:25:22.930 --> 00:25:24.470
– Huh?
– Huh?

388
00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:26.980
We order you to move
your ship outta the way!

389
00:25:26.980 --> 00:25:29.690
You're interfering with
official Navy business!

390
00:25:29.690 --> 00:25:31.790
It's your ship that's in my way.

391
00:25:31.790 --> 00:25:35.020
So I suppose it's you that's "interfering
with official Navy business."

392
00:25:35.020 --> 00:25:37.590
Uh. That's really an immature argument.

393
00:25:37.590 --> 00:25:38.830
I get what I want.

394
00:25:40.890 --> 00:25:44.060
Go, Luffy. I've bought you some time.

395
00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:45.130
Ah!

396
00:25:45.130 --> 00:25:48.800
She winked at us!
I could die of ecstasy!

397
00:25:48.800 --> 00:25:49.970
Looks like we have an opening.

398
00:25:49.970 --> 00:25:51.040
Let's set sail!

399
00:25:51.040 --> 00:25:53.190
Do you know that Warlord or something?

400
00:25:53.190 --> 00:25:57.380
Yeah, I made friends with her when
that bear guy sent me to Amazon Lily.

401
00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.810
You mean the legendary island
where only women live?

402
00:26:00.810 --> 00:26:02.080
I never believed it was a real place.

403
00:26:02.500 --> 00:26:05.630
You've been pallin' around
with the Pirate Empress?

404
00:26:05.630 --> 00:26:06.870
Come clean, now!

405
00:26:06.870 --> 00:26:09.780
You weren't really training at all
these past two years, were you?

406
00:26:09.780 --> 00:26:11.090
What else would I have been doin'?

407
00:26:11.090 --> 00:26:13.260
Damn! It's not fair!

408
00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:14.820
That would've been a
dream come true for me!

409
00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:16.220
What's his problem?

410
00:26:17.610 --> 00:26:20.520
Wow! So those are Luffy's friends!

411
00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:23.690
I've never seen so many strange
creatures together before.

412
00:26:23.690 --> 00:26:24.390
There's one...

413
00:26:24.390 --> 00:26:27.160
They look like such a fun crew!

414
00:26:27.160 --> 00:26:30.130
Okay! Everyone in position to set sail!

415
00:26:30.130 --> 00:26:31.930
– Aye, aye!
– Yes, Nami-swan!

416
00:26:31.930 --> 00:26:33.790
What's the matter, Usopp?

417
00:26:34.880 --> 00:26:36.650
Something just occurred to me.

418
00:26:36.650 --> 00:26:39.010
You never said you beat
the Navy soldiers inland.

419
00:26:39.010 --> 00:26:40.090
We didn't.

420
00:26:40.090 --> 00:26:41.990
We just flew past them,
but we could hear them shouting

421
00:26:41.990 --> 00:26:44.260
from behind us in the distance.

422
00:26:44.620 --> 00:26:47.820
Then what could be stopping
them from coming after us?

423
00:26:55.480 --> 00:26:58.920
This is backup unit Platoon
Three! Do you copy?

424
00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:02.030
We read you. What's happening?

425
00:27:02.030 --> 00:27:04.830
We are unable to reach Grove 42!

426
00:27:04.830 --> 00:27:05.830
What? Why?

427
00:27:05.830 --> 00:27:07.930
Well, because...

428
00:27:07.930 --> 00:27:10.360
There are giant bugs currently
halting our advance.

429
00:27:10.360 --> 00:27:11.670
Wait, giant what?

430
00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:17.070
These things are monsters!

431
00:27:20.420 --> 00:27:21.760
Shoot it!

432
00:27:29.200 --> 00:27:33.270
I won't let anyone get in the way
of Usopp'n goin' adventurin'.

433
00:27:36.670 --> 00:27:39.440
Men don't shed
tears when they part ways!

434
00:27:40.540 --> 00:27:43.650
Good Luck, Usopp'n.

435
00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:47.110
Who cares why they
aren't comin' after us?

436
00:27:47.550 --> 00:27:50.050
The worse their lives are,
the better ours'll be.

437
00:27:50.050 --> 00:27:52.350
Heh. It's time to get outta here.

438
00:27:52.350 --> 00:27:54.720
Nami, lead the way.

439
00:27:54.720 --> 00:27:55.520
You got it.

440
00:27:57.560 --> 00:27:58.330
All right.

441
00:28:00.850 --> 00:28:02.250
This is Platoon Four.

442
00:28:02.250 --> 00:28:03.860
Afraid I have bad news.

443
00:28:03.860 --> 00:28:07.260
All our gunpowder has been
ruined by a sudden rain shower.

444
00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.860
What?! That isn't possible.

445
00:28:09.860 --> 00:28:14.770
The forecast for Sabaody Archipelago
today is clear and sunny!

446
00:28:17.810 --> 00:28:19.940
Thunder would be excessive.

447
00:28:19.940 --> 00:28:22.810
After all, we don't wanna
scare the civilians, now.

448
00:28:22.810 --> 00:28:26.150
I wasn't expecting those bubbles
to give us so much grief.

449
00:28:26.150 --> 00:28:28.750
Bubbles or not, you can't
complain about the wind.

450
00:28:28.750 --> 00:28:32.560
No, sir, that breeze got us where
we wanted to be right on schedule.

451
00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:33.830
Well, of course it did!

452
00:28:33.830 --> 00:28:36.630
When it's something for Nami,
she gets nothing but the best.

453
00:28:40.300 --> 00:28:42.890
We'll miss you on
Weatheria, young lady.

454
00:28:42.890 --> 00:28:46.090
But get out there and give it your all!

455
00:29:02.420 --> 00:29:03.730
Hey! What's it doin'?

456
00:29:05.660 --> 00:29:08.530
Are we sure this is
supposed to inflate?

457
00:29:12.070 --> 00:29:15.070
Whoa! Now our boat's got a bubble roof!

458
00:29:15.740 --> 00:29:16.710
This is how it works.

459
00:29:17.220 --> 00:29:19.960
A ship that is properly coated
has the ability to withstand

460
00:29:19.960 --> 00:29:23.530
almost any sort of pressure,
but it also has very little buoyancy.

461
00:29:23.530 --> 00:29:27.030
The floating bag beneath the ship
is the only thing keeping us afloat.

462
00:29:27.030 --> 00:29:30.990
By deflating it, the Sunny will
become less buoyant and begin to sink.

463
00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:32.720
It's pretty simple, really.

464
00:29:32.720 --> 00:29:34.280
– Huh. Interesting.
– Huh. Interesting.

465
00:29:34.280 --> 00:29:35.620
Maybe not simple enough.

466
00:29:35.620 --> 00:29:37.720
Forget about it for now,
let's spread the sail!

467
00:29:37.720 --> 00:29:38.690
– Why?
– Why?

468
00:29:38.690 --> 00:29:40.350
We use it to catch the water current,

469
00:29:40.350 --> 00:29:42.930
similar to how we would use
the wind above sea level.

470
00:29:42.930 --> 00:29:46.370
I was hopin' we'd just sink
down to Fishman Island. Darn.

471
00:29:46.370 --> 00:29:47.570
All right!

472
00:29:47.570 --> 00:29:50.610
We'd better hurry unless we
wanna get in another fight!

473
00:29:50.610 --> 00:29:54.110
This is Central Unit
Platoon Five at Grove 42!

474
00:29:54.110 --> 00:29:55.610
We have an emergency!

475
00:29:55.610 --> 00:29:57.450
The troops from Platoon
Two have been found,

476
00:29:57.450 --> 00:29:59.830
but they've all succumbed
to a severe depression!

477
00:29:59.830 --> 00:30:02.970
Tell 'em to suck it
up and get back in the fight!

478
00:30:02.970 --> 00:30:05.800
I suck. I should've
been born a water flea.

479
00:30:05.800 --> 00:30:10.140
What we've been able to gather is that
Straw Hat Luffy flew off on a giant bird.

480
00:30:10.140 --> 00:30:11.580
So he's not even there?

481
00:30:11.580 --> 00:30:13.580
Then what are you guys shooting at?

482
00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:16.820
We are currently under
attack by unknown enemies!

483
00:30:17.260 --> 00:30:19.130
Reinforcements got here quick.

484
00:30:19.130 --> 00:30:21.130
We were just about to leave.

485
00:30:21.130 --> 00:30:22.500
Heads up!

486
00:30:24.830 --> 00:30:27.570
The Straw Hat ship is now within range!

487
00:30:27.570 --> 00:30:29.470
Uh. But we may have a problem!

488
00:30:29.470 --> 00:30:32.110
A large bird is heading
straight for us!

489
00:30:41.490 --> 00:30:42.990
Oh, wow!

490
00:30:44.530 --> 00:30:45.860
From behind, too?

491
00:30:45.860 --> 00:30:47.160
I got it!

492
00:30:49.770 --> 00:30:51.100
Like what ya see, Nami?

493
00:30:51.490 --> 00:30:56.010
I've gotten a lot stronger.
Go ahead and take it in.

494
00:30:56.010 --> 00:30:58.410
– No, not again!

495
00:31:00.890 --> 00:31:03.660
Platoon Five, come in! What's going on?

496
00:31:03.660 --> 00:31:05.770
Well, it isn't good.

497
00:31:05.770 --> 00:31:07.170
We've hit interference.

498
00:31:07.170 --> 00:31:09.110
We couldn't possibly
have anticipated this.

499
00:31:10.250 --> 00:31:11.750
Ah! Have mercy!

500
00:31:14.590 --> 00:31:17.460
How could you ever think of
turning beauties like us away?

501
00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:18.630
As if!

502
00:31:18.630 --> 00:31:20.700
Maybe they're all shy.

503
00:31:20.700 --> 00:31:23.600
There's nothing to be ashamed of, boys!

504
00:31:24.200 --> 00:31:27.140
Let's have a cup of tea!
And cookies, too!

505
00:31:27.900 --> 00:31:31.810
How awful! Truly, this
is worse than death!

506
00:31:34.440 --> 00:31:38.210
Hi, there! You've got
such an adorable face!

507
00:31:38.210 --> 00:31:39.350
Ah! No! Let me go!

508
00:31:42.070 --> 00:31:43.140
What's wrong now?

509
00:31:43.140 --> 00:31:46.480
Platoon Five, finish your report!

510
00:31:46.760 --> 00:31:49.020
This is for you, Sanji. Make it count!

511
00:31:51.780 --> 00:31:54.380
Whoa, whoa! Take it
easy, Sanji! Breathe!

512
00:31:54.380 --> 00:31:56.910
Oh. Usopp. It's you.

513
00:31:56.910 --> 00:32:00.920
Sorry, it felt like someone had
gotten a death grip on my heart.

514
00:32:00.920 --> 00:32:01.920
Bag's deflated!

515
00:32:01.920 --> 00:32:04.360
Awesome! You guys ready?

516
00:32:04.360 --> 00:32:06.990
Yeah, we're all set!

517
00:32:06.990 --> 00:32:08.330
That it, Nami?

518
00:32:08.330 --> 00:32:11.060
Yeah. Just say the word, Captain.

519
00:32:17.750 --> 00:32:18.920
All right.

520
00:32:23.630 --> 00:32:25.150
Listen up, guys!

521
00:32:25.150 --> 00:32:27.790
There's a lot I wanna say,
but we don't have much time.

522
00:32:28.970 --> 00:32:30.670
One thing can't wait, though.

523
00:32:30.670 --> 00:32:33.670
What you went through these past
two years was selfish of me,

524
00:32:33.670 --> 00:32:35.480
so thanks for puttin' up with it.

525
00:32:35.480 --> 00:32:38.020
You make it sound like this
has never happened before.

526
00:32:38.020 --> 00:32:39.170
That's no joke!

527
00:32:39.170 --> 00:32:41.700
You've always been a
selfish piece of work.

528
00:32:45.940 --> 00:32:49.550
Rear Admiral!
The pirate ship is submerging!

529
00:32:49.550 --> 00:32:50.880
We can't wait!

530
00:32:50.880 --> 00:32:54.720
Listen, you have no idea how
dangerous those pirates are!

531
00:32:54.720 --> 00:32:57.150
Move your ship! Now. Pretty please?

532
00:32:57.150 --> 00:32:59.590
– Yes, please?
– Yes, please?

533
00:32:59.960 --> 00:33:02.530
Take care of yourself, Luffy.
